            <ArticleTitle>Tuboovarian abscess caused by Candida in a woman with an intrauterine device.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Candida infection should be considered in an individual with a pelvic abscess that is unresponsive to conventional antibiotic therapy, particularly in the presence of an intrauterine device. We present a case of a tuboovarian abscess caused by Candida species in a woman with an intrauterine device for &gt;10 years. Surgical intervention followed by antifungal therapy resulted in a favorable outcome.</AbstractText>
